{
	"description": "More test vectors for word lists (VoiceFlow Android 0.8.2, plan phase 4). `merge`: cases in the same shape as merge.json (edits out of order and repeated, time offsets and ties, case and spacing, duplicates, undo chains, a fix that loses one heard form). `prompt`: the vocabulary prompt and keywords built from merged words: `terms` as in a snapshot (with the layer each came from), the budget, the app dictated into, and the exact result: the one-line `prompt`, the words `sent` (prompt order) and the request's `keywords`. `split` (VoiceFlow Desktop 0.9.15, Android 0.8.5): the transcription request and the tidy-up list from the same words. The request (`prompt`, `sent`, `keywords`) carries only the first 20 words chosen (`TRANSCRIBE_TERMS`, a code constant; the app's own words first, then priority), with hints fitted to that line within `promptChars`; `tidyWords` is every word chosen within `promptChars` and `promptTerms`, most important first, as the tidy-up lists them (3,000-character list budget). Synthetic words only. Every client that merges profiles or builds the prompt should pass them.",
	"merge": [
		{
			"name": "edits in any order, one listed twice, give the same result",
			"user": "sam",
			"ops": [
				{ "schema": "voiceflow-op", "version": 1, "id": "dev2-c", "device": "dev2", "createdAt": "2026-11-17T10:02:00Z",
					"type": "tombstone", "target": "dev1-a" },
				{ "schema": "voiceflow-op", "version": 1, "id": "dev1-b", "device": "dev1", "createdAt": "2026-11-17T10:01:00Z",
					"type": "term", "term": { "text": "Flumox" } },
				{ "schema": "voiceflow-op", "version": 1, "id": "dev1-a", "device": "dev1", "createdAt": "2026-11-17T10:00:00Z",
					"type": "term", "term": { "text": "Quibbit" } },
				{ "schema": "voiceflow-op", "version": 1, "id": "dev1-b", "device": "dev1", "createdAt": "2026-11-17T10:01:00Z",
					"type": "term", "term": { "text": "Flumox" } }
			],
			"expect": { "terms": { "dev1-b": "Flumox" }, "corrections": [], "issues": [], "rejected": [] }
		},
		{
			"name": "an edit made offline arrives late: the newer createdAt wins, not the order received",
